    "href": "/developers/webapp-workflow/",
    "searchText": "change the hosted webapp work on proctor's react and vite browser application without duplicating api, localization, routing, or design-system authority. change the hosted webapp the private webapp package builds the browser application shipped beside the server binary. it owns browser routing, same-origin transport, credential-safe client behavior, locally generated design tokens, and feature presentation. the server remains authoritative for application state, authentication, authorization, and the public http contract. prepare the package use the pinned node version and committed lockfile: for product-backed development, start the server and dependencies from the repository root, then run vite in another terminal: see local setup for ports, generated state, and origin-sensitive flows. find the feature owner feature modules live under webapp/src/features . reusable presentation proven by real feature consumers lives under webapp/src/components . a component or feature with non-obvious behavior keeps a nearby contract.md . location owns --- --- src/features/ route orchestration, transport calls, feature state, and recovery behavior src/components/ repeated visual or interaction behavior with real consumers src/api/generated generated typescript api schema; never hand-edit src/generated/i18n generated browser localization catalog; never hand-edit src/app/routes.ts generated route adapter; never hand-edit design-system/tokens.mjs human-owned product tokens and theme definitions src/styles reset, generated tokens, and document-level base styles keep route modules thin. feature-specific values, validation, asynchronous state, and recovery stay with the feature rather than being pushed into a generic form or page shell. implement a browser change 1. read the feature and component contracts that already own the flow. 2. list loading, success, empty, validation, denied, expired, unavailable, and retry states before changing the visual surface. 3. reuse the owned button, inputfield, icon, and accesspageshell components only where their contracts apply. 4. call the typed same-origin api adapter. do not duplicate server validation or authorize from client state. 5. add visible copy to the server-owned webapp. localization namespace and regenerate the typed catalog. 6. add focused unit tests and browser tests for the complete interaction. 7. review responsive layout, keyboard order, focus, reduced motion, light and dark themes, failure recovery, and localization growth. keep generated adapters current run the focused generator when its source changes: the normal gate regenerates and rejects drift. generated files are reviewable outputs, not alternate authoring locations. for a design-token change: product components consume the webapp token system. they do not import the documentation site's docusaurus tokens or add a second palette inside feature styles. run focused checks during implementation: before handoff, run the complete package gate: it validates brand assets and design tokens, checks api, localization, and route generation, type-checks, lints, runs unit and browser suites, and builds the production bundle. browser review matrix exercise every changed state at minimum in: - chromium, firefox, and webkit through the pinned playwright suite; - keyboard-only navigation and visible focus; - a narrow mobile viewport and a desktop viewport; - light and dark themes; - reduced motion; and - long localized text without clipping or layout escape. do not use hover as the only disclosure, disable browser zoom, place secrets in urls or storage, or treat a successful transport response as proof that an authorization decision was correct. next - coordinate an http contract change. - select the repository verification level. - update public documentation for released reader-visible behavior."
